course: dictionary
lesson: 2537
title: When untrue words cause harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Defamation is a word for saying or writing something untrue about a person that damages their good name. The sentence gives the clues: «Printing harmful lies about a person can be against the law; it is called defamation.» Harmful lies and against the law tell you that defamation is serious and wrong.
explain: Always check a new word by swapping in your meaning. Try it: «Printing lies that damage a person's good name can be against the law.» The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Defamation can be written or spoken. Written defamation is called libel, and spoken defamation is called slander. In news and law lessons, you may read «sue for defamation», which means taking someone to court because of untrue harmful words.
fact: Defamation means saying or writing something untrue about a person that damages their good name.
fact: Defamation is an uncountable noun, so you say «defamation» without adding -s, as in «a defamation case».
fact: Written defamation is called libel; spoken defamation is called slander.
fact: «Sue for defamation» means taking someone to court because of untrue words that harm a person.
fact: A court can make the person who printed the harmful lies pay money to the person who was harmed.
exercise: «Printing harmful lies about a person can be against the law; it is called defamation.» What is defamation? | Printing a photo of a famous person | *Saying or writing something untrue that damages a person's good name | Saying something nice about a person in the newspaper | Telling the truth about someone in a kind way
exercise: Written defamation is called what? | Slander | Rumour | Gossip | *Libel
exercise: Ella says, «The paper printed false lies about my friend, so she is going to sue for defamation.» Why might her friend sue? | *The paper spread untrue things that harmed her friend's good name | The friend won a prize | The paper was too big | Ella wants a free newspaper
test: In «a defamation case», what is the case about? | The cost of a new house | A lost pet dog | *Untrue things said or written that damage a person's good name | A football match result
test: Spoken defamation is called what? | Defamation of character | Gossip | Libel | *Slander
exam: What is the best meaning of defamation? | *Saying or writing something untrue that damages a person's good name | Saying something true and kind about someone | Making a loud noise in court | Writing a letter to a newspaper
